    <string name="privacy_policy_text" formatted="false">Sudoku is 100% ad-free and contains no advertising or analytics SDKs.&#10;&#10;What we collect: to run the global leaderboards the app signs you in with Firebase Anonymous Authentication, which creates a random user ID. When you finish a puzzle, your score (grid size, difficulty, points, time, moves, mistakes, completion date) and an automatically generated display name are stored in Google Cloud Firestore; you may optionally replace the automatic name with a nickname of your choice, which is shown publicly on leaderboards and tournaments. We do not collect your name, email address, contacts, location or photos.&#10;&#10;Purchases: in-app purchases are processed by Google Play. We never see or store your payment details.&#10;&#10;On your device: game progress, lives, purchases status and settings are stored locally and are removed when you clear the app\'s data or uninstall it.&#10;&#10;Third parties: Google Firebase and Google Play process data under Google\'s privacy policy (https://policies.google.com/privacy), which may include device and network information needed for security and reliability.&#10;&#10;Children: the app does not knowingly collect personal information from children.&#10;&#10;Contact: to ask a question or request deletion of your leaderboard data, use the developer email shown on the app\'s Google Play page.</string>

